Purpose: typed fast native calls (JS_NewCFunctionFast, a JS_CFUNC_fast prototype with a JSCFunctionFastDef signature: f64, i32, u32,
  bool and borrowed buffer arguments, the opaque of a `this` of one class) taken straight from OP_call / OP_call_method without a stack
  frame or conversion calls, with the generic function for every other call (V8 fast API calls for an interpreter); and two borrowed
  accessors that never throw: JS_GetBufferData (the bytes of an ArrayBuffer, typed array or DataView) and JS_GetFastArray (the values
  of a dense Array). Zinc binds its __host_* rows of numbers and booleans this way (src/qjs/qjs.cpp), ZN-596.
Measured: bench/qjs_boundary (M1 Pro, another tree building: indicative), ns per call over the empty loop, generic -> fast: 4 doubles
  on a method 49 -> 40, 1 int on a method 34 -> 31, int + Float32Array 50 -> 40, a global with 4 doubles 43 -> 34; the engine's
  zinc:gfx rows __host_gfxWidth() 53 -> 27, __host_gfxEase(i, d) 64 -> 40, __host_gfxSetTransform(6 doubles) 72 -> 43. Calls of
  other functions: unchanged within noise. Behaviour: tests/t0/qjs_fastcall.sh (tests/native/qjs_fastcall.c).
Upstream: prepared for quickjs-ng, not opened yet (the owner's step: the command and the text are in the notes of ZN-596).

